        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Nomadic confederation</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">209 BCE – 1757 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Power held by</span><span class="info-stat-val">A supreme ruler from one ruling clan (the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chanyu">chanyu</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">khagan</a> or khan), with princes, tribal chiefs and appointed commanders governing the wings and units of the army</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Legitimacy from</span><span class="info-stat-val">A mandate from Heaven (Tengri) granted to the ruling clan, proved by victory and by the plunder, tribute and trade the ruler shared with his followers</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">How rulers are chosen</span><span class="info-stat-val">Raised by an assembly of the ruling family and chiefs, the Mongol <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurultai">kurultai</a>, from among the founder’s descendants, often after a contest among kinsmen decided by war</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Famous examples</span><span class="info-stat-val">the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu Empire</a> (209 BCE–48 CE), the Hunnic Empire under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-turkic-khaganate">First Turkic Khaganate</a> (552–603), the Uyghur Khaganate (744–840), the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a> (1206–1368), the Dzungar Khanate (1634–1757)</span></div>
